@* POPIA privacy notice, in plain language. Mirrors the POPIA register in docs/DATA_MODEL.md;
   keep the two in step when a field is added. Not legal advice. *@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "POPIA privacy notice";
    ViewData["BackUrl"] = Url.Action("Index", "Home");
    ViewData["ScreenClass"] = "ep-screen--page";
}
<partial name="~/Views/Shared/Partials/_TopBar.cshtml" />

<div class="ep-screen__body">
    <p class="ep-card__text">This explains what eProcure collects, why, and who can see it. It is written in plain language and is not legal advice.</p>

    <section class="ep-card">
        <h2 class="ep-card__title">What we collect</h2>
        <p class="ep-card__text">Your account: full name, email address, cellphone number (suppliers verify it with a one-time code), a <em>hash</em> of your password (never the password itself) and your role. Your supplier profile: the date you gave POPIA consent.</p>
        <p class="ep-card__text">Your company: legal name, CIPC registration number, SARS tax PIN, CSD number, B-BBEE level, enterprise size (EME, QSE or generic) and sector. Your applications: your answers to the SBD questions, the payment reference and the documents you upload.</p>
        <p class="ep-card__text">For accountability we record who did what and when, with the IP address, in an audit log. We never collect card numbers, bank details, ID numbers, home addresses or dates of birth.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="ep-card">
        <h2 class="ep-card__title">Why we collect it</h2>
        <p class="ep-card__text">To sign you in, keep each organisation's information separate, check whether you meet a tender's requirements, receive and evaluate your application, confirm your tender fee through the payment provider, and keep a trustworthy procurement record.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="ep-card">
        <h2 class="ep-card__title">Who can see it</h2>
        <p class="ep-card__text">You can see your own account, company and applications. The organisation that posted a tender sees your company, application and documents only after your tender fee has cleared. Other organisations and other suppliers never see them.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="ep-card">
        <h2 class="ep-card__title">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p class="ep-card__text">Procurement, payment and audit records are kept for the public-sector records-management period. Uploaded documents are stored outside the public website and are only released after a check that you are allowed to see them.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="ep-card">
        <h2 class="ep-card__title">Questions and your rights</h2>
        <p class="ep-card__text">You may ask to see or correct your information, or ask how long it is kept. Contact the eProcure platform operator through the programme contact channel supplied by your organisation.</p>
    </section>
</div>
